{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     pagination — ported from NSDS templates/pagination.html.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Ghost's own {{pagination}} helper renders Casper's markup, not NSDS's, so
     this is written out rather than delegated. Prev/next only: Ghost gives
     {{page}} and {{pages}} but no page list, and building one from a range
     needs a helper the platform does not ship.

     The direction icon carries no label; the text for a screen reader is the
     visually-hidden span beside it. rel=prev/next is what tells a crawler
     these are one sequence.

     ⚠ NEVER WRITE {{#pagination}} IN THIS FILE. It is not a block helper —
     {{pagination}} is Ghost's own helper and what it DOES is render this
     partial. Calling it from inside here is unbounded recursion, and the
     symptom is not a template error but a 500 with
     "Maximum call stack size exceeded" and error.hbs served in place of the
     listing. This file did exactly that, and it was invisible for as long as
     the site had no published posts: with an empty collection the {{#if
     posts}} branch never reached the include, so every listing looked fine.
     The first published post broke /blog/ and would have broken every other
     listing with it.

     So the pagination data is read as PROPERTIES of the template's context —
     `pagination.pages`, `pagination.page`, `pagination.prev` — never through
     the helper. A dotted path is unambiguously a property lookup in
     Handlebars, so it cannot resolve to the helper by accident. `page_url` IS
     a real helper and is fine; it takes the page number as an argument.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#if pagination.pages}}
    <nav aria-label="{{t "Pagination"}}">
        <ul class="ns-pagination">
            {{#if pagination.prev}}
                <li><a class="ns-pagination__link" href="{{page_url pagination.prev}}" rel="prev">
                    {{> "icons/caret-left"}}<span class="ns-visually-hidden">{{t "Previous page"}}</span>
                </a></li>
            {{/if}}

            <li><span class="ns-pagination__ellipsis">{{t "Page"}} {{pagination.page}} / {{pagination.pages}}</span></li>

            {{#if pagination.next}}
                <li><a class="ns-pagination__link" href="{{page_url pagination.next}}" rel="next">
                    <span class="ns-visually-hidden">{{t "Next page"}}</span>{{> "icons/caret-right"}}
                </a></li>
            {{/if}}
        </ul>
    </nav>
{{/if}}
